  "id": "COMPOUND:27898 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound Aconitane-3,8,13,14,15-pentol,1,6,16-trimethoxy-4-(methoxymethyl)-20-methyl-, 8-acetate14-benzoate, (1a,3a,6a,14a,15a,16b)- and M-phase phosphoprotein 8, as it is a target of multiple compounds that act on the same cellular pathway. Specifically, this compound is a target of Centaurein, Sagittasine C, and (-)-Licarin B, all of which are known to interact with M-phase phosphoprotein 8. These findings indicate that the compound may exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of the cell cycle, particularly at the M-phase. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong, consistent relationship, but further validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and the compound's role in the biological process. The presence of multiple targets in the same pathway supports the hypothesis that this compound may influence the cell cycle by modulating M-phase phosphoprotein 8, though the precise mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
